The Track B escape hatch also fails the in-context-attack requirement. For the paper’s constructive Lemma 4.1 identity, repeated Jacobi expansion gives the witness directly as an alternating telescoping sum in linear time; “try alternating coefficients along the adjoint chain” succeeds rather than failing. Hiding that sum behind a dense coordinate change would turn the task into generic linear algebra and discard the paper’s native Lie structure. I’m recording this as a Step-0 rejection with the exact theorem boundary and the viable/nonviable formulations.
